(verb
  :name "circular-list"
  :std "SRFI-1"
  :library "list"
  :tier "core"
  :kind "constructor"
  :signature "(circular-list x ...) -> circular-list"
  :summary "Builds a circular list where the last cdr points back to the head. The structure is not a proper list, dotted list, or null list."
  :explanation "circular-list creates a data structure where the last element's cdr points back to the first element, forming an infinite cycle. This is distinct from proper lists, dotted lists, and null lists. The conformance suite verifies that (eq? a (cadddr x)) holds for x = (circular-list a b c), demonstrating the cycle closure. This verb exists to model cyclic data structures where elements reference themselves or each other in a loop. The `!` verbs operate on these structures by mutating the cons cells directly, so any variable holding one of these structures must be considered destroyed after mutation. The failure mode occurs when a caller continues using the original binding after mutation, which may have been cut, relinked, or overwritten under it."
  :examples (
    (:dialect "motoi" :tier "novice" :code "(circular-list 1 2 3)" :note "PENDING-ENGINE")
    (:dialect "motoi" :tier "intermediate" :code "(let ((x (circular-list 'a 'b 'c)))\n  (list (eq? 'a (car x)) (eq? 'a (cadddr x))))" :note "PENDING-ENGINE")
    (:dialset "motoi" :tier "expert" :code "(define (cycle-length lst)\n  (if (not (circular-list? lst)) #f\n      (let loop ((n 0) (current lst))\n        (if (eq? current lst)\n            n\n            (loop (+ n 1) (cdr current))))))\n(cycle-length (circular-list 1 2 3))" :note "PENDING-ENGINE")
  )
  :caveats ("DIVERGENCE from SRFI-1: The spec pack shows that circular-list is not a list?, proper-list?, or dotted-list?." "The structure forms an infinite cycle, so operations like length+ return #f.")
  :drawbacks ("Cannot be used with verbs that expect proper lists or null lists." "The cyclic nature makes some list operations undefined or infinite.")
  :usecases ("Modeling cyclic data structures where elements reference themselves." "Implementing algorithms that require circular references.")
  :related ("list" "proper-list?" "dotted-list?" "null-list?" "length+")
  :learn (:concept "Circular data structures and their properties." :prerequisites ("list" "car" "cdr") :progression "Learn about proper lists and dotted lists before working with circular lists.")
  :provenance "SRFI-1; implemented lib/std/srfi-1.js (surface completion 2026-08-02); documented against observed runtime behavior 2026-08-02"
